  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116404",
      "title": "Extracting Dynamic Route Parameters via Inputs",
      "lectureOrder": 274,
      "videoOrder": 262,
      "sourceHash": "14743ec28a235f889235bd5b5b2494039965e2e7393023c6c42f8d4b9f98163a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.67,
          "en": "So the next goal is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "to actually extract this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 10.38,
          "en": "dynamic path parameter value from the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 12.87,
          "en": "when that component here is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.87,
          "end": 16.23,
          "en": "so that we can get the actual user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.23,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "for which this component was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 21.153,
          "en": "and use it inside of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.53,
          "end": 25.08,
          "en": "And there are different ways of achieving this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.08,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "And as a Angular developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 29.49,
          "en": "you should know about all these different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.49,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "because chances are high",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 33.57,
          "en": "that you'll see these different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 35.373,
          "en": "in different projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.6,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "Now, the easiest way of getting hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "of such a path parameter value in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 46.59,
          "en": "that's loaded for a dynamic route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "is to add an input to that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "that has the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "as your dynamic path parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 58.41,
          "en": "So here I chose userId, written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "hence I would add userId, written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 64.32300000000001,
          "en": "so written in the same way, as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.28,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "for example, with the input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.92,
          "en": "cue this user tasks component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 71.94,
          "en": "And you could of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.94,
          "end": 74.493,
          "en": "also use the input decorator instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 77.1,
          "en": "And I'll make this a required input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.1,
          "end": 80.07,
          "en": "and make it clear that it'll be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.07,
          "end": 83.61,
          "en": "because these URL encoded values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "will always be strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "because the entire URL is one long string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 92.43,
          "en": "Now for this approach to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.43,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "we need to go to our application config though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "because there you need to tell the Angular router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 105.35,
          "en": "that you want to use this input based approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 108.50999999999999,
          "en": "And you do that by going to provide router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.50999999999999,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "And then there as a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113.94,
          "en": "you pass the result of calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 116.673,
          "en": "with component input binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "which is a function that must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "And this function will in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "create a configuration object you could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 129.66,
          "en": "that's passed to provide router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.66,
          "end": 131.64,
          "en": "as a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.64,
          "end": 134.836,
          "en": "or as any argument as long as it's not the first one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.836,
          "end": 137.16,
          "en": "because that must be the routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.16,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "that will tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 142.893,
          "en": "that you want to have this input binding approach enabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "With that configuration added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 150.99,
          "en": "you can go to your user tasks component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.99,
          "end": 155.99,
          "en": "and there this user ID input will then be set by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "Therefore, we can now use this user ID here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 161.76,
          "en": "to retrieve the name of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.76,
          "end": 164.52,
          "en": "because that is what I wanna output here in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.52,
          "end": 165.813,
          "en": "of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 171.09,
          "en": "Now to get the username, I have this user's service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 173.43,
          "en": "which in the end is just a dummy wrapper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 176.01,
          "en": "around this dummy user's array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.01,
          "end": 177.72,
          "en": "which I have in a separate file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.72,
          "end": 180.24,
          "en": "And of course, in a real, you might be fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.24,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "that data from a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.1,
          "end": 184.53,
          "en": "You might be sending an HTTP request there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.53,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "But to keep things simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 188.88,
          "en": "and focus on the routing in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "I'm just using the dummy file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 193.41,
          "en": "and this dummy service that gives me the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193.41,
          "end": 195.663,
          "en": "from that file through a getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 199.71,
          "en": "So we need to inject this user's service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.71,
          "end": 201.57,
          "en": "into this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 201.57,
          "end": 204.87,
          "en": "Hence I'll add a private property user's service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.87,
          "end": 208.05,
          "en": "and I'll inject it with the inject function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.05,
          "end": 210.573,
          "en": "as we did it many times before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 211.65,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "So of course, both the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 216.063,
          "en": "and the inject function are imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.159,
          "end": 219.06,
          "en": "And then we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 219.06,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "get our user name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 224.64,
          "en": "by setting up a computed property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 226.44,
          "en": "with the computed function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 226.44,
          "end": 228.423,
          "en": "since I'm dealing with a Signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.1,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "And then here we could use our user's service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 236.28,
          "en": "access to users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 239.7,
          "en": "and find the user with a specific ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.7,
          "end": 242.34,
          "en": "Find, of course we'll execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.34,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "which we pass to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 247.2,
          "en": "on every user in that user's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 247.2,
          "end": 249.45,
          "en": "And we get that user as an input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 249.45,
          "end": 251.19,
          "en": "And I then wanna return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 251.19,
          "end": 254.76,
          "en": "if the ID of the user I'm currently looking at in this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 254.76,
          "end": 257.44,
          "en": "is equal to this .userId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 258.60699999999997,
          "end": 261.753,
          "en": "and we have to read this like this since it's a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 263.37,
          "end": 265.5,
          "en": "That will give me the entire user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.5,
          "end": 268.17,
          "en": "Here I'm just interested in the name though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 268.17,
          "end": 272.343,
          "en": "so I will call name on the result of calling find.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 273.72,
          "end": 275.67,
          "en": "Though this question mark here is needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 275.67,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "because find could of course yield undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 281.90999999999997,
          "en": "if we don't find a user for that ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.90999999999997,
          "end": 284.97,
          "en": "With that though, we can go back to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.97,
          "end": 288.21,
          "en": "and instead of outputting users here as a placeholder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.21,
          "end": 292.26,
          "en": "we can now output the user name like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 292.26,
          "end": 293.58,
          "en": "reading it as a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.58,
          "end": 296.88,
          "en": "since I'm dealing with signals in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.88,
          "end": 299.55,
          "en": "But of course, just to be very clear about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 299.55,
          "end": 300.72,
          "en": "you could absolutely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.72,
          "end": 303.75,
          "en": "also build this application without signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 303.75,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "routing does not require them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 308.67,
          "en": "With that, however, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 308.67,
          "end": 311.79,
          "en": "you should see the username being reflected here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 311.79,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "And of course, as you switch between different users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 317.34,
          "en": "that name changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.34,
          "end": 319.92,
          "en": "And that's therefore one way of extracting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 319.92,
          "end": 323.55,
          "en": "and using the data that is encoded in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.55,
          "end": 326.22,
          "en": "when working with dynamic routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 326.22,
          "end": 329.64,
          "en": "It's, in my opinion, the most convenient way of doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 329.64,
          "end": 331.293,
          "en": "but it's not the only way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
